{"outcome":"built","summary":"I built a two-storey workbench organizer. Each storey has two side-by-side north-half bases. The top storey holds two full-height bins, and the bottom storey has two drawers. All open faces are capped and the joints are bolted. The check found no rule issues and no mesh collisions. The build has 34 parts, which the configurator estimates at about 2,090 g of filament and 2,971 minutes of printing.

A full base can't stand on a half base (the configurator only allows the same kind on top), and drawers only fit on the cut face of a half base. So both storeys use half bases.

To show what it's for, I put screws and nuts in two compartments of the 2-way bin, where they sit below the rim. A pen and a paint brush stand in the 3-way bin. A screwdriver, file, hex driver and standoffs wouldn't stay in place, and pliers and a tape measure wouldn't fit in the closed drawers, so I left those out.","requirements":[{"requirement":"Two storeys","status":"met","evidence":"Half bases at levels 0 and 1 in cells (0,0) and (1,0), stacked: piece:0,0,0, piece:1,0,0, piece:0,0,1, piece:1,0,1."},{"requirement":"Bins on top","status":"met","evidence":"bin:0,0,1~hex-bin-half-n-full-div2 and bin:1,0,1~hex-bin-half-n-full-div3 on level 1."},{"requirement":"A drawer below","status":"met","evidence":"drawer:0#0,0#cut and drawer:0#1,0#cut on the cut faces of the level-0 half bases."},{"requirement":"All edges capped","status":"met","evidence":"capOpenFaces added 10 solid end caps. check_build reports no open faces and no issues. lockJoints was also run."}]}
